{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CebtNUwa8MY7YZf3cxA3v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: needs_more_evidence\nCONSENSUS_BLOCKING: yes\nRATIONALE: Mercury alleges a concrete break (guard at doctrine-review.js:166-170 suppressing `fourth_shape_unclassified` when `fourthShapeCount === 0`) but never quotes the test assertion it claims is violated, and its only execution evidence is a run_check that failed with exit_code=127 — command-not-found, an environment failure, not a test failure, and model-sandbox run_check carries no test authority regardless. Telemetry shows only 5 files opened, yet Mercury claims \"examined 9 of 9\" while listing 10 candidates — an internal contradiction that overstates coverage. Its \"AST EVIDENCE\" section cites application functions (`sectionPresent`, `sectionValue`) as if they were AST scans; telemetry shows zero AST-capable tool calls succeeded (find_regex was rejected as an unknown tool; no serena_*, rule_scan, or find_references calls). Finally, the substantive merit is contestable: if `fourthShapeCount === 0` there may be nothing to classify, so \"classified 0 of 0\" could be complete rather than an absence — Mercury's proposed fix (`|| fourthShapeCount === 0`) would tag an absence on every clean diff, which may itself be the wrong semantics. Mercury also unilaterally declared UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY, which requires quoted Mercury/Fable/Kimi seats and an actual non-convergence; a single-seat allegation cannot invoke it.\nDISAGREEMENT: Mercury's claim that the test \"caps incomplete doctrine evidence with named absences instead of refusing the run\" expects `fourth_shape_unclassified` in a zero-fourth-shape fixture is unsupported — no test lines quoted, no successful test execution, and the intended semantics of the `fourthShapeCount > 0` guard may be deliberate (nothing added → nothing unclassified). Also disagree with Mercury's \"examined 9 of 9\" claim (10 listed, 5 opened per telemetry) and with labeling regex/section-string checks as \"AST-backed.\"\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: (1) Quote verbatim the full test block in test/mercury-doctrine-extension.test.js for \"caps incomplete doctrine evidence with named absences instead of refusing the run\", including its fixture diff/answer and its expected absences array. (2) Quote verbatim trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js lines 155-180. (3) Diagnose run_check exit 127 and re-run with the project's actual test runner (e.g., `node --test test/mercury-doctrine-extension.test.js`), labeling execution provenance.\nRECHECK_PROMPT: \"Open test/mercury-doctrine-extension.test.js and quote the entire test titled 'caps incomplete doctrine evidence with named absences instead of refusing the run' — the fixture inputs (diff, answer, telemetry) and every expected absence tag, with line numbers. Then quote trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js lines 155-180 verbatim. State explicitly: does the fixture contain zero added throws/gates/guards/fallbacks, and does the expected-absences assertion include 'fourth_shape_unclassified' in that zero-count case? If yes, the break stands; if the fixture has fourthShapeCount > 0 or does not assert that tag, retract the break. Separately, your npm test run_check exited 127 (command not found) — identify the correct test command from package.json, re-run it, label its execution provenance as model-sandbox, and report the actual failing assertion output if any. Do not declare UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY unilaterally.\"\nNEXT_CHECK: Host-attested run of the project's test command (from package.json scripts) filtered to test/mercury-doctrine-extension.test.js, to confirm whether the named test actually fails at HEAD.\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 12 of 12 available evidence items (no repo access in this pass): (1) Mercury answer body, (2) Mercury CANDIDATE SET list (10 files: mercury.ignore, no-banned-report-language.json, 3 test files, adversarial-review.js, ask.js, doctrine-review.js, react-loop.js, run-ledger.js), (3) Mercury's cited doctrine-review.js:166-170 guard claim, (4) Mercury's cited test lines 45-50, (5) tool telemetry (9 calls, 7 ok), (6) failed run_check exit_code=127 + artifact path ogz-meta/cognition-history/mercury-execution/2026-09-01T01-54-26-757Z-test-run.log:1-18, (7) failed find_regex call, (8) files_opened=5 count, (9) host-attested evidence manifest = none, (10) Mercury's proposed patch snippet, (11) Mercury's unilateral UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY declaration, (12) absent run ledger. M equals the full evidence set supplied; the host-supplied diff touched-file count (per Mercury: 9) is covered inside item (2) but cannot be independently verified without repo tools.\nAST EVIDENCE: Named absence. Telemetry shows zero successful AST-capable tool calls (no serena_blast_radius, serena_property_refs, serena_method_callers, serena_class_fields, find_definition, find_references, or rule_scan; find_regex rejected as unknown tool). Mercury's \"AST EVIDENCE\" section cites runtime helper functions inside doctrine-review.js, which is code-under-review, not scan evidence. AST evidence for changed JS files and touched config-key names: absent.\nINHERITED: Cannot independently enumerate without repo access. Mercury asserts \"no inherited defaults, swallowed catches, bypass env reads, or silent defaults\" across all 9-10 touched files but opened only 5 files per telemetry — the inherited sweep for mercury.ignore, no-banned-report-language.json, react-loop.js, run-ledger.js, adversarial-review.js, ask.js is unreceipted. Mark inherited status for all touched files: UNVERIFIED, unfixed by definition.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 1 of 1 candidate gate visible in evidence: the guard `if (fourthShapeCount > 0 && ...)` at claimed doctrine-review.js:166-170 — classification contested: Mercury treats it as a producer-fixable defect; plausibly it is an intentional true-boundary guard (zero additions → zero classification obligation). Unresolvable without the quoted test assertion. Mercury's proposed replacement gate (`|| fourthShapeCount === 0`) is unclassified by Mercury and appears to fire on every clean diff — flagged as a potential over-broad fallback.\nALLEGATIONS: Mercury's break allegation: SUBSTANTIVE, basis TESTIMONY-leaning — the guard citation is a code-at-HEAD claim (RECEIPT if the quoted lines are accurate) but the failing-test claim rests on an unquoted assertion plus an exit-127 non-run (no receipt). My allegations against Mercury: (a) candidate-set count contradiction (9 claimed, 10 listed, 5 opened) — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (telemetry); (b) AST evidence mislabeled — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (telemetry); (c) test-expectation unquoted — SUBSTANTIVE, RECEIPT (answer text absence); (d) improper unilateral UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (doctrine format).\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: none — the alleged break vs. intentional-guard question is a genuine substantive fork, but it is not yet a seat non-convergence; it requires the recheck evidence first. It must not be escalated to UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY on Mercury's single-seat say-so.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: Mercury's full answer including its candidate set, cited line ranges (doctrine-review.js:166-170, 51-119, 144-149, 186-190, 214-215; test lines 45-50), its proposed patch; tool telemetry including the two failed calls and the run_check exit-127 artifact reference; the empty host-attested evidence manifest; the missing run ledger.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: Actual source of doctrine-review.js, test/mercury-doctrine-extension.test.js, or any of the other 8 touched files (no repo tools in this pass); the run_check log artifact contents; package.json test script; the actual diff; git history for the change.\nASSUMED: Telemetry counts (9 calls, 5 files opened, exit 127) are accurate host reporting; Mercury's quoted line ranges refer to real locations even though I cannot verify them; exit_code=127 means the sandbox lacked npm/the command rather than a genuine test failure; the diff touched-file count of 9 supplied via Mercury's answer approximates the host's true count."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12065,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12065},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-09-01T01:55:47.857Z","request_id":"req_011CebtNSZSu97zFaCBiAdck"}
